--  "content": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"font-size:clamp(14px, 0.875rem + ((1vw - 3.2px) * 0.588), 20px);line-height:1.5\">Key indicators for Bangladesh&#8217;s development and humanitarian sector. Each figure shows its unit, period, geography and source.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Indicator</th><th>Value</th><th>Period</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Purchasing Managers&#8217; Index (PMI), overall</td><td>51.8 (48.6 in September)</td><td>October 2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/11/pmi-october-2026-economy-returns-to-expansion-mcci-policy-exchange/\">MCCI and Policy Exchange Bangladesh</a></td></tr><tr><td>Measles deaths this year</td><td>1,289 (241,556 suspected cases)</td><td>To 10 Nov 2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/11/measles-deaths-1289-241556-suspected-cases-november-10/\">DGHS, via The Business Standard</a></td></tr><tr><td>Dengue deaths this year</td><td>481 (157,628 cases)</td><td>To 12 Nov 2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/13/dengue-1960-admissions-481-deaths-november-12/\">DGHS, via The Business Standard</a></td></tr><tr><td>NGO registrations cancelled</td><td>722</td><td>2009 to 2024</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/11/722-ngo-registrations-cancelled-15-years-home-minister-parliament/\">Home Minister in Parliament, via NTV</a></td></tr><tr><td>Poverty rate, US$3.00 a day line</td><td>10.1% (about 2.1 million more people than FY25)</td><td>FY26, estimate</td><td><a href=\"https://documents.worldbank.org/en/publication/documents-reports/documentdetail/099124110052619383\">World Bank, Bangladesh Development Update, Oct 2026</a></td></tr><tr><td>Poverty rate, national line</td><td>22.5% (18.7% in 2022)</td><td>FY26, estimate</td><td><a href=\"https://documents.worldbank.org/en/publication/documents-reports/documentdetail/099124110052619383\">World Bank, Bangladesh Development Update, Oct 2026</a></td></tr><tr><td>Spending on energy and fertiliser subsidies and social protection</td><td>3.5% of GDP (US$17.4 billion)</td><td>Annual</td><td><a href=\"https://documents.worldbank.org/en/publication/documents-reports/documentdetail/099124110052619383\">World Bank, Bangladesh Development Update, Oct 2026</a></td></tr><tr><td>Poorest households outside any safety net</td><td>About half</td><td>2022 survey data</td><td><a href=\"https://documents.worldbank.org/en/publication/documents-reports/documentdetail/099124110052619383\">World Bank, Bangladesh Development Update, Oct 2026</a></td></tr><tr><td>Children reached by new World Bank primary education programme</td><td>About 26 million</td><td>Approved 6 Nov 2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/07/world-bank-300-million-primary-education-bangladesh/\">World Bank, via The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>10-year-olds who cannot read a simple, age-appropriate text</td><td>About 50%</td><td>Latest World Bank estimate</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/07/world-bank-300-million-primary-education-bangladesh/\">World Bank, via The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>Workers in the informal sector</td><td>About 84% (roughly 58 million people)</td><td>2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/05/world-bank-bangladesh-working-age-population-peaks-2045/\">World Bank, Demographic Change in South Asia</a></td></tr><tr><td>Year the working-age share of the population peaks</td><td>2045</td><td>Projection</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/05/world-bank-bangladesh-working-age-population-peaks-2045/\">World Bank, Demographic Change in South Asia</a></td></tr><tr><td>Garment minimum wage</td><td>Tk 12,500 a month (workers&#8217; side proposes Tk 32,000)</td><td>Proposal 9 Nov 2026; new scale due December</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/10/garment-workers-propose-tk-32000-minimum-wage-board/\">The Business Standard; The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>Energy-sector climate finance received as loans</td><td>92% of about US$2.54 billion</td><td>2002-2023</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/10/energy-climate-finance-92-percent-loans-change-initiative-study/\">Change Initiative, via The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>Cost of the Health National Adaptation Plan</td><td>About US$1.4 billion (Tk 17,000 crore)</td><td>2026-2031</td><td><a href=\"/2026/10/29/climate-health-plan-needs-1-4-billion-over-five-years-study-finds/\">BRAC University C3ER study, Oct 2026</a></td></tr><tr><td>Secondary teachers with health education training</td><td>30.1% of those surveyed</td><td>2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/10/29/only-30-of-secondary-teachers-trained-in-health-education-study-finds/\">DSHE school health study, with UNESCO</a></td></tr><tr><td>ADB loan for social protection reforms</td><td>US$250 million</td><td>Approved 24 Apr 2026</td><td><a href=\"https://www.adb.org/news/adb-approves-250-million-loan-implement-social-protection-reforms-bangladesh\">ADB</a></td></tr><tr><td>Widow allowance expansion under the ADB programme</td><td>At least 250,000 more women</td><td>Target</td><td><a href=\"https://www.adb.org/news/adb-approves-250-million-loan-implement-social-protection-reforms-bangladesh\">ADB</a></td></tr><tr><td>Internet users</td><td>82.8 million (47.0% of people)</td><td>Late 2025</td><td><a href=\"https://datareportal.com/reports/digital-2026-bangladesh\">DataReportal, Digital 2026</a></td></tr><tr><td>GDP growth projection</td><td>3.4%</td><td>FY26 and FY27</td><td>World Bank, Bangladesh Development Update, Oct 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Non-performing loan ratio</td><td>33.2%</td><td>June 2026 (30.6% in Dec 2025)</td><td>World Bank, Bangladesh Development Update, Oct 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Rohingya JRP appeal</td><td>USD 710.5 million</td><td>2026</td><td>Joint Response Plan 2026 update</td></tr><tr><td>Change in JRP appeal</td><td>26% lower than 2025</td><td>2026 vs 2025 (USD 934.5 million)</td><td>Oxfam, Aug 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Share of 2025 JRP appeal funded</td><td>46%</td><td>2025</td><td>Oxfam, citing OCHA</td></tr><tr><td>Rohingya refugees in Bangladesh</td><td>Nearly 1.2 million</td><td>2026</td><td>Oxfam</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n