---  "content": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"font-size:clamp(14px, 0.875rem + ((1vw - 3.2px) * 0.588), 20px);line-height:1.5\">Key indicators for Bangladesh&#8217;s development and humanitarian sector. Each figure shows its unit, period, geography and source.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Indicator</th><th>Value</th><th>Period</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Purchasing Managers&#8217; Index (PMI), overall</td><td>51.8 (48.6 in September)</td><td>October 2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/11/pmi-october-2026-economy-returns-to-expansion-mcci-policy-exchange/\">MCCI and Policy Exchange Bangladesh</a></td></tr><tr><td>Measles deaths this year</td><td>1,289 (241,556 suspected cases)</td><td>To 10 Nov 2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/11/measles-deaths-1289-241556-suspected-cases-november-10/\">DGHS, via The Business Standard</a></td></tr><tr><td>Dengue deaths this year</td><td>481 (157,628 cases)</td><td>To 12 Nov 2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/13/dengue-1960-admissions-481-deaths-november-12/\">DGHS, via The Business Standard</a></td></tr><tr><td>NGO registrations cancelled</td><td>722</td><td>2009 to 2024</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/11/722-ngo-registrations-cancelled-15-years-home-minister-parliament/\">Home Minister in Parliament, via NTV</a></td></tr><tr><td>Poverty rate, US$3.00 a day line</td><td>10.1% (about 2.1 million more people than FY25)</td><td>FY26, estimate</td><td><a href=\"https://documents.worldbank.org/en/publication/documents-reports/documentdetail/099124110052619383\">World Bank, Bangladesh Development Update, Oct 2026</a></td></tr><tr><td>Poverty rate, national line</td><td>22.5% (18.7% in 2022)</td><td>FY26, estimate</td><td><a href=\"https://documents.worldbank.org/en/publication/documents-reports/documentdetail/099124110052619383\">World Bank, Bangladesh Development Update, Oct 2026</a></td></tr><tr><td>Spending on energy and fertiliser subsidies and social protection</td><td>3.5% of GD