--+  "content": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"font-size:clamp(14px, 0.875rem + ((1vw - 3.2px) * 0.588), 20px);line-height:1.5\">Key indicators for Bangladesh&#8217;s development and humanitarian sector. Each figure shows its unit, period, geography and source.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Indicator</th><th>Value</th><th>Period</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bank credit growth, private sector vs government</td><td>Private sector 4.09%; net credit to government 36.34%; total domestic credit 11.18%</td><td>Sept 2026 over Sept 2025</td><td><a href=\"https://www.bb.org.bd/pub/weekly/selectedindi/15_november%202026.pdf\">Bangladesh Bank, Selected Economic Indicators</a></td></tr><tr><td>Inflation and wage growth</td><td>Inflation 8.27% (food 6.40%, non-food 9.89%; rural non-food 10.21%); wage rate index 7.63%</td><td>October 2026</td><td><a href=\"https://thefinancialexpress.com.bd/economy/inflation-dips-to-827pc-in-october-as-food-prices-ease\">BBS, via The Financial Express</a></td></tr><tr><td>Classified (bad) loans</td><td>32.78% of total outstanding loans (15.22% net)</td><td>June 2026</td><td><a href=\"https://www.bb.org.bd/pub/weekly/selectedindi/15_november%202026.pdf\">Bangladesh Bank</a></td></tr><tr><td>Rohingya children aged 6 to 59 months with acute malnutrition</td><td>14.6% (8.6% in 2024, 13.9% in 2025); 42.6% stunted</td><td>2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/14/rohingya-food-aid-funded-until-april-2027-rations-malnutrition/\">Nutrition SMART Survey 2026, via The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>People with diabetes who do not know they have it</td><td>67% of women, 72% of men</td><td>2022</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/14/diabetes-seven-in-10-unaware-bdhs-world-diabetes-day/\">BDHS 2022 (NIPORT), via The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>Climate adaptation finance: need vs international money</td><td>About US$8.5 billion a year needed; around $4 billion available, under $0.5 billion from international sources; 88% of adaptation spending from the national budget</td><td>Annual, stated Nov 2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/13/cop31-bangladesh-adaptation-need-8-5-billion-under-half-billion-international/\">Environment Ministry and UNDP, COP31 side event</a></td></tr><tr><td>Animal vaccine doses made in Bangladesh</td><td>32 crore of about 260 crore needed a year (12.31%); imports cost about Tk 5,000 crore a year</td><td>Latest DLS data, Nov 2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/14/government-plans-tk-300-crore-animal-vaccine-plant-cut-imports/\">Department of Livestock Services, via The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>Purchasing Managers&#8217; Index (PMI), overall</td><td>51.8 (48.6 in September)</td><td>October 2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/11/pmi-october-2026-economy-returns-to-expansion-mcci-policy-exchange/\">MCCI and Policy Exchange Bangladesh</a></td></tr><tr><td>Measles deaths this year</td><td>1,304 (245,562 suspected cases; 25,028 confirmed)</td><td>15 Mar to 13 Nov 2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/14/measles-deaths-1304-245562-suspected-cases-november-13/\">DGHS, via The Business Standard</a></td></tr><tr><td>Dengue deaths this year</td><td>507 (165,644 hospitalised this year; 5,609 in hospital)</td><td>To 17 Nov 2026</td><td><a href=\"https://bdnews24.com/health/r25qs7p03d\">DGHS, via bdnews24.com</a></td></tr><tr><td>NGO registrations cancelled</td><td>722</td><td>2009 to 2024</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/11/722-ngo-registrations-cancelled-15-years-home-minister-parliament/\">Home Minister in Parliament, via NTV</a></td></tr><tr><td>Poverty rate, US$3.00 a day line</td><td>10.1% (about 2.1 million more people than FY25)</td><td>FY26, estimate</td><td><a href=\"https://documents.worldbank.org/en/publication/documents-reports/documentdetail/099124110052619383\">World Bank, Bangladesh Development Update, Oct 2026</a></td></tr><tr><td>Poverty rate, national line</td><td>22.5% (18.7% in 2022)</td><td>FY26, estimate</td><td><a href=\"https://documents.worldbank.org/