-+  "content": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"font-size:clamp(14px, 0.875rem + ((1vw - 3.2px) * 0.588), 20px);line-height:1.5\">Calls for proposals, grants, tenders and expressions of interest relevant to organisations working in Bangladesh. Every listing shows the funder, size, deadline and status, and links to the original notice.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Open now</h2>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"color:#5c5c5c;font-size:14px\">Last checked: 18 November 2026.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Opportunity</th><th>Funder</th><th>Size</th><th>Deadline</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.ungm.org/Public/Notice/322127\">Evaluation and impact assessment for mental health programmes in Bangladesh (RFP-SEARO-Bangladesh-2026-013)</a><br><small>Tender for firms and organisations with evaluation and research capacity. Eligibility details are in the RFP documents on UNGM. Deadline 14:00 Dhaka time.</small></td><td>World Health Organization (WHO) Bangladesh</td><td>Not stated</td><td>25 Nov 2026</td><td><strong>CLOSING SOON</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://www.ungm.org/Public/Notice/322642\">Two External National Collaborators for the EPZ Model Zone Initiative with BEPZA (rfx_14397_ROAP)</a><br><small>For individual national consultants. Published on UNGM on 16 November. Deadline 11:30, listed as GMT+1.</small></td><td>International Labour Organization (ILO) Bangladesh</td><td>Not stated</td><td>26 Nov 2026</td><td><strong>CLOSING SOON</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://www.apn-gcr.org/news/2026-call-for-proposals-under-the-crrp-and-capable-programmes/\">2026 call for proposals: Collaborative Regional Research (CRRP) and Scientific Capacity Development (CAPaBLE)</a><br><small>For researchers and practitioners at institutions in APN member and approved countries, including Bangladesh. South Asia themes include climate resilience and loss and damage, nature-based solutions, and food, water and energy security. Summary proposals first, by 23:59 Japan time (20:59 Dhaka); full proposals by invitation.</small></td><td>Asia-Pacific Network for Global Change Research (APN)</td><td>Not stated</td><td>30 Nov 2026</td><td><strong>OPEN</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://www.yves-rocher-fondation.org/en/how-to-apply-for-the-international-award/\">Terre de Femmes International Award 2027: \"Trees in the City\"</a><br><small>Open worldwide. Projects led by a woman or group of women, run through a non-profit at least one year old. The foundation's page is headed 2027 but gives a 2026 deadline, so confirm with the funder.</small></td><td>Yves Rocher Foundation</td><td>EUR 10,000 each (2 winners)</td><td>30 Nov 2026</td><td><strong>OPEN</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://d-prize.org/\">D-Prize: funding to start organisations that distribute proven poverty solutions</a><br><small>For new organisations, usually under 18 months old and under $30,000 raised. No country restrictions listed. The regular deadline passed on 15 November; the extension deadline needs registration and closes at midnight Pacific Time.</small></td><td>D-Prize</td><td>Up to $20,000</td><td>6 Dec 2026</td><td><strong>OPEN</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://www.adb.org/news/events/community-resilience-partnership-program-partnership-forum-2027-call-solutions\">Community Resilience Partnership Program Forum 2027: call for solutions</a><br><small>One-page proposals on locally led climate and health adaptation from practitioners in South Asia, Southeast Asia and the Pacific; women especially encouraged. ADB pays travel for selected presenters to the forum in Bangkok on 23 and 24 February 2027. Not a project grant.</small></td><td>Asian Development Bank (ADB)</td><td>Travel support</td><td>15 Dec 2026</td><td><strong>OPEN</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://innovation.wfp.org/wfp-innovation-challenge\">WFP Innovation Challenge</a><br><small>Equity-free funding for organisations with an innovation at least at minimum viable product stage. Applications are accepted on a rolling basis.</small></td><td>World Food Programme (WFP) Innovation Accelerator</td><td>Not stated</td><td>Rolling</td><td><strong>OPEN</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Recently closed</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Opportunity</th><th>Funder</th><th>Deadline</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"/2026/10/29/open-call-global-eba-fund-medium-size-grants-of-up-to-500000-for-ecosystem-based-adaptation/\">Medium-size grants for ecosystem-based adaptation</a></td><td>Global EbA Fund (IUCN, UNEP; IKI funding)</td><td>16 Nov 2026</td><td>CLOSED</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.undp.org/press-releases/innovators-wanted-undp-launches-usd-1-million-global-challenge-healthier-ocean\">Ocean Innovation Challenge, 5th call: marine pollution, coastal restoration and blue economy</a></td><td>UNDP, funded by Sida</td><td>15 Nov 2026</td><td>CLOSED</td></tr><tr><td>Small-size grants for ecosystem-based adaptation</td><td>Global EbA Fund</td><td>26 Oct 2026</td><td>CLOSED</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://asiapacific.unwomen.org/en/programme-implementation/2026/09/unw-ap-bgd-cfp-2026-003-addressing-the-medium-to-long-term-reintegration-needs-and-strengthening-social-protection-support-mechanisms-for-the-social-inclusion-of-bangladeshi-migrants\">Reintegration and social protection for Bangladeshi women migrants (CSO partner)</a></td><td>UN Women Bangladesh</td><td>15 Oct 2026</td><td>CLOSED</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How we list opportunities</h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>We link to the funder&#8217;s own notice wherever one exists.</li>\n\n\n<li>Status labels are OPEN, CLOSING SOON (seven days or less), UPCOMING and CLOSED. We never describe an expired call as open.</li>\n\n\n<li>Each listing shows the date we last checked it. Deadlines can change, so always confirm with the funder.</li>\n\n\n<li>Featured placement may be paid for in future. Paid listings will always be labelled and will never change a listing&#8217;s status or details.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Funding Tracker</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We are building a tracker of who funds what in Bangladesh: major donors, thematic priorities, humanitarian and development financing, climate finance and localisation. Read our first funding analysis on the <a href=\"/2026/10/29/rohingya-response-the-2026-appeal-is-a-quarter-smaller-and-still-underfunded/\">Rohingya response appeal</a> and the <a href=\"/2026/10/29/new-atlantic-council-brief-examines-bangladeshs-changing-aid-landscape/\">changing aid landscape</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"/submit/\">Submit a funding opportunity</a> · <a href=\"/category/funding/\">All funding coverage</a></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-color wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"color:#5c5c5c;font-size:14px\">Top image: the Sundarbans mangrove forest. Photo: Amdadphoto / <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mangrove_River_Maze.jpg\">Wikimedia Commons</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>.</p>\n\n\n",
