d from social protection</td><td>71.0% (46.5% of beneficiaries did not meet the poverty criteria); programmes reach about three in 10 households</td><td>Published 18 Nov 2026</td><td><a href=\"https://www.adb.org/publications/adaptive-social-protection-bangladesh-report\">ADB, Strengthening Adaptive Social Protection in Bangladesh</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Classified (bad) loans</td><td>32.78% of total outstanding loans (15.22% net)</td><td>June 2026</td><td><a href=\"https://www.bb.org.bd/pub/weekly/selectedindi/15_november%202026.pdf\">Bangladesh Bank</a></td></tr><tr><td>Rohingya children aged 6 to 59 months with acute malnutrition</td><td>14.6% (8.6% in 2024, 13.9% in 2025); 42.6% stunted</td><td>2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/14/rohingya-food-aid-funded-until-april-2027-rations-malnutrition/\">Nutrition SMART Survey 2026, via The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>People with diabetes who do not know they have it</td><td>67% of women, 72% of men</td><td>2022</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/14/diabetes-seven-in-10-unaware-bdhs-world-diabetes-day/\">BDHS 2022 (NIPORT), via The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>Climate adaptation finance: need vs international money</td><td>About US$8.5 billion a year needed; around $4 billion available, under $0.5 billion from international sources; 88% of adaptation spending from the national budget</td><td>Annual, stated Nov 2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/13/cop31-bangladesh-adaptation-need-8-5-billion-under-half-billion-international/\">Environment Ministry and UNDP, COP31 side event</a></td></tr><tr><td>Animal vaccine doses made in Bangladesh</td><td>32 crore of about 260 crore needed a year (12.31%); imports cost about Tk 5,000 crore a year</td><td>Latest DLS data, Nov 2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/14/government-plans-tk-300-crore-animal-vaccine-plant-cut-imports/\">Department of Livestock Services, via The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>Purchasing Managers&#8217; Index (PMI), overall</td><td>51.8 (48.6 in September)</td><td>October