--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/data/posts/garment-unrest-640-factories-shut-union-leaders-arrested-wage-board-23-november.json
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+{
+ "slug": "garment-unrest-640-factories-shut-union-leaders-arrested-wage-board-23-november",
+ "date": "2026-11-19T07:20:00",
+ "modified": "2026-11-19T07:20:00",
+ "title": "Wage unrest shuts about 640 factories; two union leaders arrested",
+ "excerpt": "Garment workers protested for a second day after the wage board meeting was moved to 23 November. Police arrested two federation leaders in Pallabi.",
+ "categories": [
+  "news"
+ ],
+ "tags": [
+  "garments",
+  "poverty-reduction-decent-employment",
+  "human-rights",
+  "governance-human-rights",
+  "women-empowerment"
+ ],
+ "image": null,
+ "content": "<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">About 640 garment factories were disrupted on Tuesday (17 November) as wage protests spread for a second day, The Financial Express reported, citing the Bangladesh Garment Manufacturers and Exporters Association (BGMEA). Of these, 115 were closed under the \"no work, no pay\" rule and 525 declared a holiday. Workers took to the streets after the Minimum Wage Board postponed its 16 November meeting to 23 November.</p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Protests continued on Wednesday. In Ashulia, 132 factories were shut and workers vandalised MK Apparels, The Business Standard reported. Police arrested Mosammat Sultana Begum, central president of the Green Bangla Garments Workers Federation, and its general secretary Md Ilyas in Pallabi, accusing them of threatening owners and stirring up workers.</p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Police used tear gas and sound grenades on protesters at Hemayetpur in Savar and at Jamgora and Narsingpur in Ashulia, bdnews24.com's Bangla edition reported. In Kafrul, police and workers clashed after allegations that local BNP leaders had harassed women workers, The Business Standard reported. A 27-year-old worker, Hawa Begum, was hit in the hand by a rubber bullet.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The wage gap</h3>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Workers are asking for a minimum wage of Tk 32,000 a month. The new wage is due to take effect from 1 December, with the first payment in January 2027, according to The Financial Express.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why it matters</h3>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Most garment workers are women, and many live on wages that have trailed prices for years. The arrest of union leaders, factory closures under \"no work, no pay\" and the use of force at protests raise labour-rights and civic-space concerns for rights groups, legal aid NGOs and organisations working with women workers in Savar, Ashulia and Gazipur.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What to watch</h3>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The wage board meeting on 23 November, whether the two federation leaders get bail, and whether more factories close under the \"no work, no pay\" rule.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Sources</h3>\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://today.thefinancialexpress.com.bd/first-page/rmg-turmoil-spills-into-day-two-640-units-shut-1794936066\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Financial Express: RMG turmoil spills into day two, 640 units shut, 18 November 2026</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.tbsnews.net/economy/rmg/2-labour-leaders-among-3-held-unrest-leads-closure-132-rmg-factories-ashulia-1606536\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Business Standard: 2 labour leaders among 3 held as unrest leads to closure of 132 RMG factories in Ashulia, 18 November 2026</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.tbsnews.net/bangladesh/police-garment-workers-clash-kafrul-over-alleged-harassment-female-workers-1606131\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Business Standard: Police, garment workers clash in Kafrul over alleged harassment of female workers, 18 November 2026</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://bangla.bdnews24.com/samagrabangladesh/hf9memvl9b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">bdnews24.com (Bangla): Garment workers protest in Savar and Ashulia, 18 November 2026</a></li>\n</ul>"
+}
